<topic xml:id="rt-hardware-testing-tool-options"
       role="reference" xml:lang="en"
       xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.2"
       xmlns:its="http://www.w3.org/2005/11/its"
       xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude"
       xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
       xmlns:trans="http://docbook.org/ns/transclusion">
  <info>
    <title><command>hwlatdetect</command> and <command>cyclictest</command> command-line options</title>
    <!-- can be changed via merge in the
      assembly -->
    <!--add author's e-mail address-->
    <meta name="daria.vladykina@suse.com" content="" its:translate="no"/>
    <abstract>
      <para>
        Real-time latency measurement tools support multiple runtime parameters. This section
        provides a structured reference table of the command-line options for
        <command>hwlatdetect</command> and <command>cyclictest</command>. These parameters help you
        customize sampling duration, sample windows and thread execution.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <para>
    The <command>hwlatdetect</command> and <command>cyclictest</command> commands support several
    configuration options to modify their behavior.
  </para>
  <table xml:id="tab-hwtest-hwlat-options">
    <title><command>hwlatdetect</command> options</title>
    <tgroup cols="2">
      <colspec colname="col_opt" colwidth="1*"/>
      <colspec colname="col_desc" colwidth="2*"/>
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry>Option</entry>
          <entry>Description</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--duration</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Run the detector logic for the specified duration.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--threshold</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Specify the TSC gap used to detect an SMI.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--hardlimit</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Define the failure limit.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--window</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Specify the size of the sample window.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--width</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Specify the sampling duration within the window.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--report</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Specify the output file name of the detector report.
                    </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--debug</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Turn on debug output.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--quiet</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>Turn off information output.</entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--watch</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Print sample data to standard output as it arrives.
                    </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </tgroup>
  </table>
  <table xml:id="tab-hwtest-cyclictest-options">
    <title><command>cyclictest</command> options</title>
    <tgroup cols="2">
      <colspec colname="col_opt" colwidth="1*"/>
      <colspec colname="col_desc" colwidth="2*"/>
      <thead>
        <row>
          <entry>Option</entry>
          <entry>Description</entry>
        </row>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--nsec</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Use nanoseconds instead of microseconds for the displayed latency values.
                    </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--loops</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Limit the number of test cycles. By default, the tool runs forever.
                    </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--threads</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Specify the number of threads. Without a number, <command>cyclictest</command> runs on all 
                        available processors.
                    </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--affinity</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Pin test threads to the processors with the same thread number.
                    </entry>
        </row>
        <row>
          <entry><option>--histogram</option>
          </entry>
          <entry>
                        Create a histogram with the latency values up to the maximum tracking time.
                    </entry>
        </row>
      </tbody>
    </tgroup>
  </table>
</topic>
